        "extract_protocol_ch1": [
          "Peripheral blood mononuclear cells (PBMCs) were isolated from whole blood by a standard Ficoll-Paque (GE Healthcare, Uppsala, Sweden) density gradient centrifugation, frozen in freezing media, and stored in liquid nitrogen tank until use.",
          "Freshly frozen PBMCs were thawed in a water bath at 37oC for 1 min, transferred to a 50-ml tube, and ten volumes of warm RPMI 1640 medium with 10% FCS and 0.1mg/ml DNase I were added slowly, followed by centrifugation at 300g for 5 min. The cell pellet was collected and cell number and viability were determined using trypan blue on Luna-II automated cell counter (Logos Biosystems). Each PBMC sample was labelled with respective sample multiplexing antibody (Single-Cell multiplex kit - Human; BD Biosciences) and then up to 6 samples were pooled together at equal numbers of 10,000 cells to make up 60,000 cells in total and loaded on a microwell cartridge of the BD Rhapsody Express system (BD Biosciences). Single cell whole transcriptome analysis libraries were prepared according to the manufacturer\u2019s instructions using BD Rhapsody WTA Reagent kit (BD, 633802)."
        ],
